# Run by set_spec.py (exec, in its namespace): the civic townsfolk of each people, the foe families, the bestiary,
# beasts and mounts, and the large creatures. Coverage first (one of everything a published adventure calls for),
# variety second: `prio` orders the painting queue (2 = one of each staple foe, 3 = the bestiary's staples,
# 4 = heroes, 5 = townsfolk and beasts, 5.5 = the rest of the bestiary, 6 and up = horde variants).
# Only folklore creatures and ones in the open D&D System Reference Document; no publisher's protected monsters.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ a core civic set for EACH people (7 x 10 = 70)
